+//AI(W906-INDEX-BOOTENABLE) 20261004: NB2-1 C1-4 (machine dispatch 7 A4-5 / A5-2; NIGHT_REPORT s0 #93 = A, Steven 1004 07:2x).
+//  golden builds MTestY1 / MTestZ1 / MTestZ2 / MTestY2 as TMyGALILMotor with Enable=true on a ship build (above, :3947-3958).
+//  HT9050 has no Galil card: Index Z1 runs on the 1203 through the Galil route (EtherCAT/Pci1203GaliRoute.cpp), and Y1 / Z2 / Y2
+//  do not exist (Mot_Table M13 / M15 / M16: SMC, Enable 0). Until now only a SUCCESSFUL route install disabled them
+//  (W906_GaliRouteDisableAbsentIndexAxes, 0930 D1 = A) -- with no route (card not usable, control not armed, monitor not up) they
+//  stayed "enabled with no card" and the full HOME looped silently at steps 375 (Z2) and 1250 (A4-5): Gali_SingalHome waits for a
+//  lamp no scan ever updates. Now, on an HT9050 only, an Index axis whose Mot_Table row is missing or Enable 0 is built
+//  Enable=false here, at boot -- the disabled-axis path golden itself takes (Gali_SingalHome myGALILmotor.cpp:4647 "done").
+//  An axis with an enabled row stays golden (Enable=true); the route installer still runs its D1 (now a no-op for these).
+//  HT9050 = the tree's run-time test (ArmCellPlan.h ArmCellIsHt9050): GPIB model 9050GPIB (database.cpp:318, read by
+//  LoadMachineConfig before InitialMotorParameter) or MachineTypeChoice == Type_HT9050. Each disabled axis prints one line.
+#include <cstdio>
+bool W906_Ht9050IndexAbsentAtBoot(int motIndex, bool hasRow, int rowEnable)
+{
+    if (!(W906_GpibModel == "9050GPIB" || MachineTypeChoice == Type_HT9050)) return false;   // every other machine: golden
+    if (hasRow && rowEnable != 0) return false;
+    std::printf("[index] HT9050: MOT[%d] %s has no enabled Mot_Table row -> Enable=false at boot (s0 #93 = A)\n",
+                motIndex, (motIndex >= 0 && motIndex < TOTAL_MOTOR) ? MOT[motIndex].Alias.c_str() : "?");
+    return true;
+}
